  "tagline": "Tencent's mmap-backed key-value store for mobile apps, built as a faster SharedPreferences/NSUserDefaults.",
  "description": "MMKV is a small key-value storage framework from Tencent's WeChat team. It memory-maps a file, encodes values with protobuf and appends writes, so individual reads and writes take microseconds, and data survives crashes because the OS flushes mapped pages. It runs on Android, iOS, macOS, Windows, Linux, HarmonyOS and Flutter, supports multi-process access on Android, AES encryption and per-key expiry. It is the usual replacement for SharedPreferences, NSUserDefaults or AsyncStorage when those become a bottleneck. It is not a database for querying data: there are no indexes beyond the key.",
